The purpose should be noted here, as this actually addresses two issues:
1. When the same line is both the end of a fold and the start of another fold, it should be marked as a start to prevent the beginning of the fold from being ignored;
2. If multiple folds end at the same location, the outermost level should be used to mark the end position to prevent the end of the outer fold from being ignored;

It would be better to use the following code snippet along with the corresponding return values from the lua language server to understand this PR better:
```lua
 local function first()
  return {
    child = {
      value = true,
    } } end; local function second() return {
  child = {
    value = false,
  },
}
end
```
